From 30399eeaad3650ad7ed36940a2c0b412dbda537c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Horizon authors <>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:24:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] End the immortal hour for a lifetime below zero, so the rite
 of return can start the death at once

Saves are loaded into Jijimon's house, which arms the immortal hour, and tickDeathCondition returned
at once during it. Only the rite of rebirth writes a lifetime below zero (every other writer clamps
at 0), so tickDeathCondition now ignores the immortal hour for it.
---
 src/main/partner_impl.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main/partner_impl.c b/src/main/partner_impl.c
index 0c9fd0ee..bd57b3ba 100644
--- a/src/main/partner_impl.c
+++ b/src/main/partner_impl.c
@@ -2105,7 +2105,9 @@ void tickSicknessMechanics(void)
 
 void tickDeathCondition(void)
 {
-	if ((HAS_IMMORTAL_HOUR == 1) && (IMMORTAL_HOUR == HOUR)) {
+	/* A lifetime below zero is only written by the rite of rebirth (script 212, section 74): it ends the
+	 * immortal hour, which saves loaded in Jijimon's house start with. Every other path clamps at 0. */
+	if ((HAS_IMMORTAL_HOUR == 1) && (IMMORTAL_HOUR == HOUR) && (PARTNER_PARA.remainingLifetime >= 0)) {
 		return;
 	}
 
